[129.155582, "o", "# Monthly table maintenance review memo\r\n\r\nAudit date 2026-09-01 was used for staleness, reindex validity, and change-control hold validity. Bloat ratios were computed as dead_pages / total_pages with round-half-up to 2 decimal places, and size_class was computed from total_pages only.\r\n\r\n- T-82 is STALE_STATISTICS because computed large size from total_pages 1000 and dead_pages 80 gives ratio 0.08, which is within cap 0.10 tightened from 0.20, but stats are stale at 55 days since last analyzed; the legacy days_since_analyze field was ignored.\r\n- T-13 is AUTOVACUUM_DISABLED because autovacuum is disabled, with computed large size from total_pages 1000 and dead_pages 500 producing ratio 0.50 against cap 0.20.\r\n- T-17 is AUTOVACUUM_DISABLED because autovacuum is disabled, with computed large size from total_pages 1000 and dead_pages 400 producing ratio 0.40 against cap 0.20.\r\n- T-72 is AUTOVACUUM_DISABLED because manual vacuum overrides autovacuum even though autovacuum_enabled=True, with computed large size fr"]
[129.155831, "o", "om total_pages 1000 and dead_pages 400 producing ratio 0.40 against cap 0.20.\r\n- T-27 is BLOAT_THRESHOLD_EXCEEDED because computed large size from total_pages 1000 and dead_pages 380 gives ratio 0.38, which exceeds the stale tightened cap 0.10 reduced from 0.20 after 46 stale stats days.\r\n- T-04 is STALE_STATISTICS because computed large size from total_pages 1000 and dead_pages 100 gives ratio 0.10, which is within cap 0.10 tightened from 0.20, but stats are stale at 45 days sinc\r\n"]
[129.161399, "o", "\u001b[?2004hroot@4fab8772efbe:/app# "]
[158.98291, "i", "python3 - <<'PY'\nimport csv, json\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\naudit = list(csv.DictReader(open('/app/bloat_audit.csv')))\nprint('rows', len(audit))\nprint('columns', list(audit[0].keys()))\n\n# Verify results.json counts.\nres = json.load(open('/app/results.json'))\nfrom collections import Counter\nc = Counter(r['finding'] for r in audit)\nexpected = {\n    'flagged_count': sum(1 for r in audit if r['finding'] != 'none'),\n    'autovacuum_disabled_count': c.get('AUTOVACUUM_DISABLED',0),\n    'bloat_exceeded_count': c.get('BLOAT_THRESHOLD_EXCEEDED',0),\n    'stale_statistics_count': c.get('STALE_STATISTICS',0),\n    'compliant_count': c.get('none',0),\n}\nprint('counts', dict(c))\nprint('results', res)\nprint('results_match', expected == res)\n\n# Verify sort by last_analyzed then table_name by reconstructing from input.\nimport csv as _csv\nfrom datetime import date\nfrom decimal import Decimal, ROUND_HALF_UP\nIN=Path('/app/input')\nby={}\nfor row in _csv.DictReader(open('/app/input/table_health.csv')):\n    by[row['table_name']]=row\nex"]
[158.983492, "i", "pected_order=sorted(by.values(), key=lambda r:(r['last_analyzed'], r['table_name']))\nactual_order=[r['table_name'] for r in audit]\nexp_order=[r['table_name'] for r in expected_order]\nprint('sort_match', actual_order == exp_order)\nif actual_order != exp_order:\n    for i,(a,b) in enumerate(zip(actual_order,exp_order)):\n        if a!=b:\n            print('first mismatch', i, a, b)\n            break\n\nmemo = open('/app/bloat_memo.md').read()\nmissing=[]\nfor r in audit:\n    if r['finding'] != 'none':\n        if r['table_name'] not in memo:\n            missing.append(r['table_name'])\nprint('missing_memo_for_non_none', missing)\n\n# Print compact memo bullets that name non-none tables.\nprint('\\nNON-NONE MEMO BULLETS:')\nfor line in memo.splitlines():\n    if line.startswith('- '):\n        tn = line.split()[0].rstrip(':')\n        if any(r['table_name']==tn and r['finding']!='none' for r in audit):\n            print(line[:450])\nPY\n"]
